===================================================================
XAUDIO alpha release 2, now with Layer III
June 4th 1997

- ------------------------------------
XAUDIO Library Version 0.7 alpha
MXAUDIO Motif GUI Version 0.9 alpha
XAUDIO Windows GUI Version 0.3 alpha
XAUDIO BeOS GUI Version 0.9 alpha
===================================================================

NOTE: this is an alpha version.
      It will work in most cases, but might still contain bugs.
      It is free, and will expire on October 1st 1997

- --------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT'S NEW since release 1:

    * Layer III support (plays .mp3 files)
    * MPEG 2 support (player files encoded at 16, 22.05, and 24 kHz
    * New MIPS / Irix port 
    * Minor bug fixes


INTRODUCTION:
- -------------
      XAUDIO was written to be a fast implementation of an MPEG Audio 
      decoding library to be used by various GUI front-ends.
      We release this alpha version of the players as free download.
      They will become shareware when the first frozen version is released.

PLATFORMS:
- ----------
   This release includes static and dynamic binaries for:

      * Linux x86
      * FreeBSD x86
      * Solaris Sparc
      * Solaris x86
      * Windows 95 / Windows NT x86
      * BeOS DR9
      * Irix Mips

FEATURES:
- ---------
 
   1. XAUDIO Library
      * Portable MPEG Audio Layer I, II and III support, MPEG 1 and MPEG 2.
      * Generic audio device support & file output.
      * C code optimization (runs faster than maplay).
      * Pentium assembler optimization.
      * Tested on x86, sparc, powerPC, MIPS.
      * Full random access to the bitstream.
      * Full audio control (mono, stereo, volume, balance, etc...)
      * Error robustness.
      
   2. XAUDIO Motif GUI
      * First native GUI for a unix MPEG audio player.
      * Generic motif 1.2 calls (will run on any motif implementation).
      * Multiple dynamic panels.
      * Interactive trackbar control for direct seek.
      * Interactive audio controls.
      * Minimal playlist support (undocumented).
      
 
   3. XAUDIO Windows GUI
      * Multithreaded decoding.
      * Multiple dynamic panels.
      * Interactive trackbar control for direct seek.
      * Interactive audio controls.
      * Drag & Drop support.
      * InstallShield (tm) archive distribution.

   4. XAUDIO BeOS GUI
      * Interactive trackbar control for direct seek.
      * Interactive audio controls.
      * Drag & Drop support.
      
CURRENT DEVELOPMENTS / FUTURE PLANS:
- ------------------------------------

      * Macintosh port (coming very soon...)
      * Network Streaming TCP streaming (http, ftp) (pre-alpha stage)
      * Unicast, Multicast and Broadcast (UDP, raw or RTP)
      * RSTP Server and Client (development started)
      * Nextstep port.
      * HP-UX port.
      * Extended playlist support.
      * Linux sparc/ Linux alpha with Lesstif (waiting for audio driver). 

BUG REPORTS / INFO:
- -------------------

      * Send email to               xaudio@mpeg.org
      * Check out our web page      http://www.mpeg.org/xaudio

