Version 2.2 of sirc, an IRC client in perl, is now available.

sirc is a relatively small (around 150k) IRC client that looks and acts
a lot like ircII, has most of its features, and is written and
scriptable in perl.

It should appeal to those who want a client with all the usual features
and would rather not have it take megabytes of disk space, and to all
those perl hackers who would rather do their IRC scripts in perl than in
a specialized language.

Some of the changes in 2.2 are:

 ... support for connections through socks proxies
 ... much faster DCC SEND
 ... lots of little bugfixes and cosmetic changes
 ... increased configurability
 ... tighter integration of the scripting API, more hooks

The primary sites are

	ftp://esane.eboai.org/pub/orabidoo/sirc/
	http://www.pobox.com/~espel/sirc/

It's also been uploaded to sunsite and funet.fi.

