                     REQUEST FOR DISCUSSION (RFD)
               unmoderated group comp.os.linux.powerpc

This is a formal Request For Discussion (RFD) for the creation of a
world-wide unmoderated newsgroup comp.os.linux.powerpc. This is not
a Call for Votes (CFV); you cannot vote at this time. Procedural
details are below.

Newsgroup line:
comp.os.linux.powerpc	Discussion of Linux on PowerPC machines.

RATIONALE: comp.os.linux.powerpc

Ports of Linux to the PowerPC microprocessor have been in existence
since 1995. In the past year and a half, however, Linux on PowerPC
gained considerable momentum, with three different kernel flavors
existing concurrently: the original Linux/PPC port by Gary Thomas
running on motherboards from Motorola, Be, and IBM (home web site:
<http://www.linuxppc.org/>); the Mach microkernel-hosted "MkLinux"
port sponsored by Apple Computer and OSF that runs on some Power
Macintoshes and clones (home web site:
<http://www.mklinux.apple.com/>); and a monolithic Linux kernel port
by Paul Mackerras (home web site:
<http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~tesch/linux_info/>).

The discussions on these projects currently take place in mailing
lists dedicated to each of the ports. In recent months, people have
complained that the lists (particularly the MkLinux lists) see too
much traffic, and too many repeated questions in particular. In
addition, the current setup does not allow users of different flavors
of PowerPC Linux to interact with each other easily, when they have
much to gain from each other (all three flavors are binary compatible,
and the userland software are mostly identical). We feel that a
newsgroup will solve both of these problems.

The newsgroup is not aimed to supplant any of the existing mailing
lists, but to supplement and extend them. We believe that the
newsgroup will be a more accessible venue of discussion for many users
who cannot follow such a heavy traffic of mail, while the the quality
of the lists themselves will improve as the traffic level winds down
to a more manageable level.

The newsgroup will *not* be gated to any mailing list, or vice versa.
(Exceptions may be made for the moderated announcement lists, with
permission from the list owners.)

CHARTER: comp.os.linux.powerpc

comp.os.linux.powerpc is for discussion about Linux running on systems
based on the PowerPC microprocessor family.

The posting of commercial information to this group is permitted only
if the information is directly relevant to Linux on PowerPC. Spamming
of any sort is absolutely not tolerated.

END CHARTER.

PROCEDURE:

This is a request for discussion, not a call for votes. In this phase of
the process, any potential problems with the proposed newsgroups
should be raised and discussed. The discussion period will continue
for a minimum of 21 days (starting from when the first RFD for this
proposal is posted to news.announce.newgroups), after which a Call for
Votes (CFV) will be posted by a neutral vote taker. Please do not
attempt to vote until this happens.

All discussion of this proposal should be posted to news.groups.

This RFD attempts to comply fully with the Usenet newsgroup creation
guidelines outlined in "How to Create a New Usenet Newsgroup" and "How
to Format and Submit a New Group Proposal".  Please refer to these
documents (available in news.announce.newgroups) if you have any
questions about the process.

DISTRIBUTION:

This RFD will be posted to the following newsgroups:
  news.announce.newgroups
  news.groups
  comp.os.linux.announce
  comp.sys.powerpc.misc

and the following mailing lists:
  <mklinux-announce@mklinux.apple.com>
      subscribe via: <majordomo@mklinux.apple.com>
      (put "subscribe mklinux-announce" in the body)
  <linux-ppc@meetpoint.mcu.motsps.com>
      subscribe via: <majordomo@meetpoint.mcu.motsps.com>
      (put "subscribe linux-ppc" in the body)
  <linux-pmac@samba.anu.edu.au>
      subscribe via: <majordomo@arvidsjaur.anu.edu.au>
      (put "subscribe linux-pmac" in the body)

Proponent: Christopher Penney <penney@cps.msu.edu>
Proponent: Shimpei Yamashita <shimpei@socrates.caltech.edu>

