This is to announce the birth of a new service which should help promote
Linux in Quebec (One province of Canada). The main purpose of this new
site is not to explain how to use linux or what you can do with it: This
is already well covered over the net. The purpose of linux-quebec.org
is to answer the query "Who do what with linux around here". While this
post is "local", we figure that such a site should be imitated and
one day, a global site should allow one to find his regionnal server
easily.

This site is running "in french" but we feel it would be could to explain
what we have done. Feel free to ask me more question if you can't
understand a word from http://www.linux-quebec.org.

Mostly, linux-quebec.org is running an SQL server which classify linux
"players" in different category. One person/organisation may enter in
multiple categories (with a different description for each)

	Consultants

		Your doing some business helping people use linux

	Resellers

		You sell machine preinstalled with linux. You sell
		linux CDs, books. You sell something related to
		linux...

	Developpers

		Commercial product, free product.

	Users

		You are doing something interesting with linux

	Internet providers

		You are using linux and/or can help linux users
		to connect to the internet.

Further, there is another section where linux related jobs may be offerred
and also the counter part section where one may offer his service. 

Registering to www.linux-quebec.org is done using a Java applet. It is
free (and should remain). The participant must provide

	name/organisation name
	contact
	Postal address
	email address
	URL to his own page

Then he must fill at least one description in one of the above categories.
Inscription are stored in a temporary database and are reviewed by one
admin person and then insert in the official database. The management of
the new inscription is also done using a java program.

Participant may at any time modify their entry (even if the entry is not
yet validated). The new version goes in the temporary database, to be
reviewed again.

linux-quebec.org is also running a mailing list (ulq@linux-quebec.org) 
which should be the start of some user groups. Email to
ulq-request@linux-quebec.org to register.

So...

	-You do something with linux, register now :-)
	-You know somebody who do something with linux, push him
	 to register
	-You would like to setup something equivalent for your
	 area, then email me. You could very well use the tools
	 we have done.

This site is brand new, so is pretty empty ...

- --------------------------------------------------------
Jacques Gelinas (jacques@solucorp.qc.ca)
