This is the newest version of my binary distribution of ImageMagick
together with an updated binary package of all shared graphic libraries
needed by ImageMagick. They will move to the places listed in the
LSM-entry at the end of this message.

ImageMagick 3.8.6 brings together a number of minor changes made to
accomodate PerlMagick and WebMagick and libIMPlugIn 1.2 updates
libpng from 0.90 to 0.96 and fixes a serious bug in writing
images < 8bpp. ImageMagick 3.8.6 needs at least libIMPlugIn 1.1 to get
started, but I recommend using version 1.2 . Please read
/usr/local/doc/IMPlugIn/IMPORTANT after installing one of them.

ImageMagick (TM), version 3.8.6, is a package for display and
interactive manipulation of images for the X Window System.
ImageMagick performs, also as command line programs, among others
these functions:

   - Describe the format and characteristics of an image 
   - Convert an image from one format to another 
   - Transform an image or sequence of images 
   - Read an image from an X server and output it as an image file 
   - Animate a sequence of images 
   - Combine one or more images to create new images 
   - Create a composite image by combining several separate images 
   - Segment an image based on the color histogram 
   - Retrieve, list, or print files from a remote network site 

ImageMagick supports also the Drag-and-Drop protocol form the OffiX
package and many of the more popular image formats including JPEG,
MPEG, PNG, TIFF, Photo CD, etc.

