Description
- -----------

Bibfrm can read or create bibliographic files in the <i>bibtex</i>
format. The graphical interface enables to immediatly vizualize which of
the fields are optional or compulsory accordingly to the document type.
You can navigate through references, search for a particular string, or
sort the references on document type, authors or date. A text summary,
associated with each reference, can be typed in a text editor provided
with the interface, and then mailed to people on your pre-defined mail
list.
 
Downloading
- -----------

More information as well as the binaries can be found at :
 
	http://icps.u-strasbg.fr/~genaud/FRM/bibfrm_english.html


