TeamWave Software announces the production release of version 1.1 of
its TeamWave Workplace collaboration software.

TeamWave Workplace is an Internet groupware product that lets you work 
together with colleagues in real-time or asynchronously, using Macintosh,
Windows or Unix platforms.

TeamWave provides "shared spaces" on the Internet allowing groups
to share information.  These electronic team rooms provide places
to meet in real-time, or a common locale to leave information for
other collaborators.  TeamWave combines real-time groupware
technologies such as shared whiteboards, chat rooms, and customizable
groupware applets with a persistent work environment to support
both meetings and ongoing work.

Downloading instructions and more info at http://www.teamwave.com/.
Free time-limited demonstration licenses are available, and we are
also making TeamWave available to educational institutions for free.
Regular licenses are US$50, with quantity discounts available.

